                <pb facs="0497" n="283" sameAs="frus:frus1871/pg283"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 98.</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Washburne to Mr. Fish</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 350.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United-States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1871-01-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 23, 1871</date>. (Received February
                    17.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to send you herewith a
                    copy of a correspondence I have had with Count de Bismarck, (including one
                    letter to Mr. Motley, and one to Mr. Moran,) on the subject of my dispatch-bag
                    to and from Paris to London.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. B. WASHBURNE.</signed></closer>











